 "title": "Histone Methylation and S-adenosylhomocysteine Accumulation in Drosophila and Yeast",
 "summary": "This cluster is centered around the relationship between histone methylation and S-adenosylhomocysteine (SAH) accumulation in Drosophila and yeast. Histone methylation, catalyzed by Dot1, is inhibited by SAH, which accumulates in Drosophila and yeast. SAH also accumulates in Drosophila due to the presence of the PL methylation process. The cluster also includes various methods and tools used in the analysis of these organisms, such as Western blot analysis, Polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis, and NMR. Additionally, the cluster mentions the relationship between CVD and SAH accumulation, as well as the growth defects caused by SAHH in Canton-S and w[1118] organisms.",
